  "$comment": "german-1 (22 October 2026): the WhatsApp allergen guard's trigger words for GERMAN (de-DE, de-AT, de-CH, de-LI — one list for the language). OPTION B, as English and French: absence / safety words only — allergy and intolerance words, Zöliakie, anaphylaxis, EpiPen, the \"-frei\" / \"ohne <allergen>\" / \"frei von\" forms, \"geeignet für\" / \"sicher für\", traces and cross-contamination — NOT the bare allergen names (a presence question, \"Ist Milch im Burger?\", may reach the AI, which answers only from the tags and gets the caveat). Matched with the Unicode normaliser: lower case, accents and umlauts folded (ü → u), ß kept as a letter — so Swiss / reformed \"ss\" and old \"ß\" spellings (Nuss / Nuß) and the typed \"ue\" form (Nuesse) are each listed. The token \"frei\" mirrors English's \"free\" (a whole word only, so \"Freitag\" does not match). caveatWords: a tagged uk14 label (stored in English, lower case) → the German words a reply may use for it, including Austrian (Obers, Topfen) and Swiss (Rahm) dairy words. scripts/german-1.cjs proves it.",
